From 290a53c6138f259d3d080c9d0057e9fc838b544b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cyril Rohr <hey@cyrilrohr.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:06:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] solver: prepare mode=max cache export remotes in parallel

ExportTo walks cache records one at a time, so a mode=max export creates
the blobs of independent stages sequentially. PrepareCacheExport walks
the same records first and resolves them in parallel across independent
branches, bounded by GOMAXPROCS. Like ExportTo, a record is prepared
before its dependencies, which then usually find their blobs among the
ones created for its chain. ExportTo reuses the prepared remotes through
CacheExportOpt.Prepared instead of loading the results again; errors are
still reported by ExportTo, so the exported cache does not change.

Signed-off-by: Cyril Rohr <hey@cyrilrohr.com>
